    "display_name": "Simulating a Viral Post",
    "long_instructions": "In Lesson 8, students complete this exact task: turning a fixed-days loop into one that runs until a target is hit, using the while loop syntax from the overview you just read. This is also their first experience debugging an existing program rather than writing one from scratch.\r\n\r\nIt should simulate a post growing in views until it reaches a target number.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Update `simulate` so that it simulates how many days it will take for a viral post’s `views` to reach `target`.\r\n- Ensure that, for each day, `simulate` prints a message in the format: `\"Day {day}: {views} views\"`.\r\n- Choose and experiment with different arguments to `simulate`. Pay attention to how they change your simulation’s outcome.\r\n\r\n**🖥️ Coding Tip:**\r\n\r\nRemember that Python’s `while` loop can repeat code while a condition is true. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\ni = 1\r\nwhile i < 5:\r\n    print(i)\r\n    i += 1\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n::: details [**See a solution**]\r\n```\r\ndef simulate(views, growth, days):\r\n  for i in range(days):\r\n    print(f\"Day {i}: {views} views\")\r\n    views = views + views * growth\r\n\r\n\r\nsimulate(100, 1, 10)\r\n```\r\n\r\n:::",
